# Chaos: eased health and mana bars with a chip trail (O229; client/BASE.md "0146"; src/client/chaosbars.h (new, pure),
# creature.h/.cpp, luafunctions_client.cpp, mods/client_settings/classes/dataset.lua, options/graphics.otui; after 0001-0145).
# The bar over a creature (Creature::drawInformation) set the width of the health rect from the percent at once, so every hit
# was a jump. With the option on the bar is drawn at a displayed percent that eases to the real one and a hit leaves a pale
# segment behind it (the "chip"):
#  * chaos::bars::Track (chaosbars.h): the value last shown, the value it goes to and two start times. Everything is computed
#    from g_clock at draw time (the pattern of 0142): no timer, no event, no per-frame state to update. A bar eases to a new
#    value in 150 ms (ease-out) and reaches it exactly. A fall leaves a chip from where the bar stood (or, when a chip is on
#    screen, from where that chip is) to the new value: it holds 250 ms, then slides down in 300 ms (smoothstep). A rise eases
#    up and has no chip; an open chip is dropped.
#  * Creature::drawInformation calls m_healthBar.observe(m_healthPercent, now) when it draws the bar (and m_manaBar.observe
#    for the mana bar, local player and others), then draws the same filled rects as before: black background, the pale chip
#    rect (only when it is at least one pixel wide), the health rect at the eased width. Filled rects only: no setMark,
#    setScale, setRotation or clip, so the draw cache is not flushed.
#  * A bar that has no value yet, or was not drawn for 1 s, takes its value at once. Creature::onAppear (m_removed: a new
#    creature or one that comes back into view) and Creature::setHealthPercent (the first health, or any health while
#    m_removed) reset both tracks, so a creature never slides in from 100.
#  * Creature.setSmoothBars(bool) / isSmoothBars() (static, one switch; off in the engine, the overlay module game_visualfx
#    turns it on from the option `smoothBars`). Option off: the stock lines run, the new tracks are neither touched nor read.
#  * dataset.lua: option `smoothBars` (default on); its apply tells game_visualfx and game_chaoshud (the character plate eases
#    the same way in Lua). graphics.otui: one checkbox "Smooth health bars" under "Ambient particles"; the visual
#    effects panel grows from 295 to 314 px (19 px per row).
# Cost with the option on: one clock read and a few float operations per drawn bar, one extra filled rect while a chip shows.
# Known: bars of at most 25 px move in whole pixels, so a 1% hit is a chip of 0 or 1 px. The percent has a 1% step, so the
# ease runs between two steps of the server, not between two exact hit points.
# Checked: applies after 0001-0145 on the base tree with 0 fuzz; creature.cpp and luafunctions_client.cpp pass
# g++ -fsyntax-only with no new error (creature.cpp keeps the 3 base errors); the header passes client/tools/chaosbars_test.cpp.
# Not built, linked or run in a client; goes live with the next client build.
